        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Academy Sports + Outdoors sells treadmills in its stores and on academy.com, from budget
          walking pads to NordicTrack's top home machines. This page sets out what we could confirm on
          academy.com on 20 October 2026 — the brands listed and their prices, how bulky items are
          delivered, the assembly offer, the return window and its conditions, the price-match rules
          and the store credit card — with company facts cross-checked against independent sources.
          Individual prices change weekly, so treat the figures as a dated snapshot rather than a quote.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. Should You Buy a Treadmill at Academy Sports? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Academy is a reasonable place to buy a mainstream home treadmill, particularly if you
            live near one of its stores in the South or Southeast; its price match, which beats a
            qualifying competitor's price by 5%, is unusually generous, but its 60-day return policy
            expects the machine back unused and in its original packaging.</strong> On 20 October 2026
            academy.com listed treadmills and walking pads from NordicTrack, ProForm, Bowflex, Echelon,
            Sunny Health &amp; Fitness, XTERRA, UREVO, WalkingPad, CENTR, Assault Fitness, adidas and a
            handful of other brands, at listed prices from $199.99 to $4,999.99 for motorized machines.
          </p>
          <p>
            Three things matter more at Academy than the sticker price. First, large treadmills ship by
            Academy's bulk carrier, and the level of delivery you pick — to the door, inside the main
            entrance or to the room — changes what happens on the day. Second, Academy does not ship to
            California, Alaska or Hawaii, so outside the contiguous states minus California it is not an
            option at all. Third, the return rules are written for unused goods, so the in-store test
            matters: find out whether you like the machine before it is built in your spare room.
          </p>
          <p>
            Academy's prices are not consistently lower or higher than buying elsewhere. On the day we
            checked, one NordicTrack model was $300 cheaper at Academy than on NordicTrack's own site
            and another was $400 dearer. Compare the exact model number and the delivered price every
            time. Our <a href="/treadmill-buying-guide-2026/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill buying guide</a>
            covers what separates a good machine from a poor one.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="about-academy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. What Is Academy Sports + Outdoors, and Where Are the Stores?</h2>
<p>
            Academy Sports + Outdoors is a publicly listed sporting goods and outdoor retailer
            headquartered in Katy, Texas, just west of Houston. The company's own history traces it to a
            tire shop that Max Gochman opened in San Antonio in 1938, which moved into military surplus
            and then sporting goods; it took its current name in 1995. Its stores are large-format and
            sell everything from hunting, fishing and camping gear to footwear, team sports, grills and
            fitness equipment.
          </p>
          <p>
            Academy describes itself as operating more than 300 stores in 21 states, and independent
            reporting on its 2025 results put the count at 322 stores in 21 states before this year's
            openings. Its store directory, checked on 20 October 2026, listed the same 21 states:
            Alabama, Arkansas, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Indiana, Kansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Maryland,
            Mississippi, Missouri, North Carolina, Ohio, Oklahoma, Pennsylvania, South Carolina,
            Tennessee, Texas, Virginia and West Virginia. Texas dominates: well over a third of the
            store pages in Academy's directory are Texan, with Georgia, Florida, Alabama, Louisiana,
            North Carolina and Tennessee next. Maryland had a single store. The directory listed roughly
            345 individual store pages, a figure that may include newly opened or announced locations,
            so treat it as approximate; the company has said it plans 20 to 25 openings in fiscal 2026.
          </p>
          <p>
            For a treadmill buyer that footprint decides how useful Academy is. If you live in Texas, the
            Gulf states or the Southeast, there is probably a store close enough to try a machine before
            you buy it. In the Northeast, the upper Midwest or the West, Academy is an online retailer
            for you — and in California it is not one at all, because academy.com does not ship there.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="brands" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">3. Which Treadmill Brands Does Academy Sell?</h2>
<p>
            On 20 October 2026 Academy's treadmill category showed 94 items across four pages, including
            a few accessories (a treadmill mat and a walking pad handrail) and two stair steppers. The
            treadmills and walking pads came from the brands below. The range changes through the year
            and not every model is stocked in every store, so treat this as a snapshot of the website.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[560px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Brand</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">What we saw on academy.com (20 Oct 2026)</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Listed prices</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Our coverage</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">NordicTrack</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T Series 5, 6.5 S, 8, 10 and 16; T 7.5 and T 8.5 S; EXP 10i; Commercial 1250 and LE; Elite X16i; X22i incline trainer; Ultra 3</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$599.99 to $4,999.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700"><a href="/best-nordictrack-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Brand roundup</a> and model reviews</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">ProForm</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Cadence 4.0, Sport, Sport 3.0, Carbon TL, TLS, TLX and T10, Carbon Pro 2000 and 9000</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$399.99 to $1,799.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700"><a href="/best-proform-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Brand roundup</a></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Bowflex</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Bowflex 7, 10 and 22</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,699.99 for the 7; $2,299.00 and $2,999.00 shown for the 10 and 22, marked "Our Price In Cart"</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700"><a href="/bowflex/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Brand page</a></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Echelon</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Stride DuoPad, Stride 50-RCX, 50 RCX Pro, 4S and 8s-22</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$299.99 to $2,499.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700"><a href="/echelon-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Brand guide</a></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sunny Health &amp; Fitness</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">More than 20 models, from a manual treadmill and walking pads to auto-incline and incline/decline machines (plus one Asuna model)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$249.99 to $3,999.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">—</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">XTERRA</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">TRX1000, TRX1200, TRX1400, TR65, TR75, TR75H Hiker and WS200 WalkSlim</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$599.99 to $1,799.99, several below the stated MSRP</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">—</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">UREVO and WalkingPad</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Walking pads and compact folding treadmills</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">UREVO $199.99 to $529.99; WalkingPad $599.99 to $1,219.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700"><a href="/best-walking-pads/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Walking pad roundup</a></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">CENTR and Assault Fitness</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">CENTR Runr and Runr-S; a Centr x HYROX non-motorized curved treadmill; the AssaultRunner Pro</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,199.99 to $6,999.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700"><a href="/assaultrunner-pro-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">AssaultRunner Pro review</a> and <a href="/best-curved-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">curved treadmills</a></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Others</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">adidas T-19i and T-23, Reebok GT40x, Schwinn 810, Lifepro, Stamina, Marcy and Dynamax models</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$259.99 to $1,299.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700"><a href="/reebok-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Reebok treadmills</a></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The centre of gravity is iFIT's two brands, NordicTrack and ProForm, which between them made
            up about a quarter of the listings, and Sunny Health &amp; Fitness, which had the most models
            of any single brand. Academy's own category text names ProForm, NordicTrack, Reebok and Sunny
            Health &amp; Fitness as its headline brands. What is missing is just as telling: there was no
            Sole, Horizon, Landice or commercial club brand, so if your shortlist runs to those you will
            be buying elsewhere.
          </p>
          <p>
            Several of the NordicTrack listings use names that are easy to confuse — "T Series 5" and
            "T 5.0 S", for example, appeared as separate products at the same price. Our guide to the
            <a href="/nordictrack-t-series-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">NordicTrack T Series</a>
            explains the line-up. Always match the full item number on the Academy page (it is listed
            under "about this product") with the manufacturer's model number before you compare prices
            or ask for a price match.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="price-range" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">4. How Much Do Treadmills Cost at Academy?</h2>
<p>
            Listed prices for motorized treadmills and walking pads on academy.com ran from $199.99 (a
            UREVO under-desk walking pad) to $4,999.99 (the NordicTrack Ultra 3) on 20 October 2026. The
            single most expensive item in the category was the non-motorized Centr x HYROX curved
            treadmill at $6,999.99. Roughly, the listings fell into four tiers:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Under $500:</strong> walking pads from UREVO, Sunny, Lifepro and Echelon, a
            couple of manual or magnetic treadmills, and entry folding machines such as the ProForm
            Cadence 4.0. These suit walking far more than running.</li>
            <li><strong>$500 to $1,000:</strong> the busiest tier — entry NordicTrack T Series and
            ProForm Carbon models, most XTERRA and Sunny folding machines, adidas, Reebok and Schwinn.</li>
            <li><strong>$1,000 to $2,000:</strong> mid-range NordicTrack and ProForm, Bowflex, the larger
            Echelon models, CENTR and WalkingPad's larger machines.</li>
            <li><strong>Over $2,000:</strong> NordicTrack's Elite X16i, X22i and Ultra 3, the AssaultRunner
            Pro and the top Sunny and Echelon machines.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Two pricing details are specific to Academy. Some listings show a manufacturer's suggested
            price struck through next to Academy's price — several XTERRA models were $200 to $700 below
            the MSRP shown — and one Sunny machine was marked as a Hot Deal at $399.99, down from $499.99.
            And two Bowflex models showed a price ($2,299.00 for the Bowflex 10 and $2,999.00 for the 22)
            marked "Our Price In Cart", with a note that the manufacturer had asked Academy not to share
            the price until the item is in your cart. That is a normal minimum-advertised-price
            arrangement, not a hidden fee, but it means the figure on the listing may not be what you pay;
            add the machine to the cart before you compare it.
          </p>
          <p>
            For what each of those tiers typically buys in motor, deck and frame, see
            <a href="/how-much-does-a-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">how much a treadmill costs</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="in-store-testing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">5. Can You Try a Treadmill at an Academy Store?</h2>
<p>
            The best reason to buy from a store chain is that you can stand on the machine first, and
            Academy's stores have fitness departments. Whether a particular treadmill is on the floor,
            though, varies by store, and the website is the larger range. On the product pages we
            checked, Academy offers a "Find availability by selecting a store" option; use it, and then
            call the store to ask whether the model is assembled on the floor rather than only boxed in
            the back.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you get there, test properly. A ten-minute session tells you far more than pressing
            start for thirty seconds:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Wear your own shoes</strong> and clothes you can jog in.</li>
            <li><strong>Walk, then run</strong> at the speeds you will really use. A deck that feels roomy
            at walking pace can feel short once your stride lengthens.</li>
            <li><strong>Use the incline</strong> through the range you expect to use, and notice how
            quickly it responds.</li>
            <li><strong>Listen and feel</strong> for motor noise, frame flex and console shake at speed.</li>
            <li><strong>Fold and unfold it</strong> yourself if it folds, and check how heavy it is to move.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Our <a href="/where-to-buy-a-treadmill-near-me/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">in-store treadmill test</a>
            sets out the full protocol. Before you leave, photograph the spec card and the model number
            on the frame, and check that the machine you order has the same item number. Treadmill names
            are reused across model years with real changes underneath.
          </p>
          <p>
            At Academy the in-store test matters more than usual, because the return policy (below) is
            written for unused goods. Finding out that a machine is too loud or too short for you after it
            has been delivered and built is the expensive way to learn.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="delivery" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">6. How Does Academy Deliver a Treadmill?</h2>
<p>
            Most full-size treadmills on academy.com do not travel by parcel carrier. The product pages we
            checked said they ship "via Academy's Bulk Carrier Service" and that bulk orders cannot go to a
            PO Box or a military APO/FPO/DPO address. Academy's shipping help page, checked on 20 October
            2026, says heavy or bulky items go by a freight trucking company, usually leave the
            distribution centre within one business day and arrive within 7 to 14 business days. It lists
            three delivery levels where your order qualifies:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Basic Delivery:</strong> the carrier delivers to your door, with no appointment
            or signature required.</li>
            <li><strong>Scheduled Delivery:</strong> the carrier contacts you to book a delivery within
            the main entrance of your home.</li>
            <li><strong>Room of Choice:</strong> the carrier contacts you to book delivery to the room you
            choose.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The help page does not give prices for the three levels, and the shipping cost is calculated
            at checkout from your address, the item's size and weight and the method. Academy's free
            shipping offers (orders over $50, $25 when signed in to its free loyalty programme, or no
            minimum with its credit card) exclude large, heavy and bulk items, so do not assume a treadmill
            ships free. We could not find an independent source describing the delivery tiers, so this
            section rests on Academy's own pages; check the options and their cost at checkout for your
            ZIP code.
          </p>
          <p>
            For a box that can weigh as much as an adult, the difference between "to your door" and "to
            the room" is the whole job. If you choose basic delivery, plan who will carry the box in and
            up any stairs. Our <a href="/treadmill-delivery-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill delivery guide</a>
            explains what each level usually means on the day, and
            <a href="/how-much-does-a-treadmill-weigh/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">how much a treadmill weighs</a>
            gives typical boxed weights.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some items ship directly from the brand rather than from Academy. Academy flags these with a
            banner saying the item may ship from a different location; once such an order has been passed
            to the vendor it cannot be switched to store pick-up or a different address, and it can only
            be cancelled before the vendor accepts it. Measure the room and the route to it before ordering —
            the <a href="/treadmill-dimensions-space-requirements/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">space requirements guide</a>
            covers the clearances.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="assembly" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">7. Does Academy Assemble Treadmills?</h2>
<p>
            Sometimes. Academy's in-store services page, checked on 20 October 2026, says that when you
            buy an oversized item it will "assist with free assembly for in-store pickup or offer home
            delivery", and it names select treadmills among the products covered. In other words, the
            free assembly offer is tied to picking the machine up from a store, and it applies to some
            treadmills rather than all of them.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is worth thinking through before you rely on it. An assembled full-size treadmill is
            large, heavy and awkward, and it may not fit in your vehicle or through your front door in
            one piece; a store-built walking pad or compact folder is a different matter. On the product
            pages we checked for full-size NordicTrack, Bowflex and Sunny machines, store pick-up was not
            available for the default store, and every specification list we read said "Assembly
            Required: Yes". Ask the store whether your model qualifies, and whether you would be
            collecting it built or boxed.
          </p>
          <p>
            We did not see an in-home assembly add-on on the Academy product pages we checked. If you are
            having the machine delivered, you have three options: check whether the brand sells its own
            assembly service (NordicTrack, for example, offers delivery, assembly and haul-away for an
            extra charge when you buy direct), book a local fitness technician or assembly service, or do
            it yourself. Most home treadmills arrive with the heavy base pre-built and need the uprights,
            console and handrails attaching — a two-person job of an hour or two. Our
            <a href="/how-to-assemble-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill assembly guide</a>
            sets out the job.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="returns" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">8. What Is Academy's Return Policy on Treadmills?</h2>
<p>
            Academy's return policy, as published on academy.com on 20 October 2026, accepts returns of
            "most unused, new condition items within 60 days of purchase" and refunds to the original form
            of payment. Fitness equipment is not on its list of excluded or restricted categories, which
            covers firearms, hunting equipment, fuel-powered items, boats, trading cards and some
            electronics. An independent retail guide published in 2026 gives the same 60-day window for
            most unused items in their original packaging. For a treadmill, the conditions are what matter:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Resalable, in the original packaging.</strong> Except where there is a product
            defect, damage in transit or "a valid product performance issue", returned merchandise must
            be resalable with no visible wear or usage, in its original packaging and with all paperwork,
            parts and accessories.</li>
            <li><strong>Bulk-shipped items need Customer Care.</strong> Online orders can normally be
            returned to any store or by mail to Academy's returns centre in Katy, Texas, but the policy
            says that if you want to return a purchase "requiring special or bulk shipping", you should
            contact Customer Care. It does not say how collection works or what it costs.</li>
            <li><strong>Picked up in store, returned in store.</strong> Items bought online and collected
            from a store must be returned to a store, not by carrier.</li>
            <li><strong>Charges may not come back.</strong> Online refunds are of the purchase price "less
            other academy.com charges" unless you are eligible for a refund of those charges, so assume
            the delivery fee may not be refunded.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Read together, those terms mean a treadmill that has been assembled, used and had its box
            thrown away is unlikely to qualify for an ordinary change-of-mind return, while one that
            arrives damaged or does not work properly falls under the defect and performance exceptions.
            Keep the box and packing material until you are sure, and before buying ask Customer Care how
            a bulk item return would physically happen and whether any fee applies. One grey area: Academy
            limits returns of opened electronics to exchanges, and it is not clear from the policy whether
            a treadmill with a built-in touchscreen would ever be treated that way. Ask, and get the answer
            in writing.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some low-quality third-party pages still quote 30 or 90 days for Academy returns. Academy's own
            page said 60 days when we checked, so follow that. Our guide to
            <a href="/treadmill-return-policies/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill return policies</a>
            compares how other retailers and manufacturers handle large-item returns.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="price-match" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">9. Does Academy Price Match Treadmills?</h2>
<p>
            Yes, and it goes further than most: Academy's price-match guarantee, checked on 20 October 2026,
            says it will <strong>beat</strong> a qualifying competitor's advertised price by 5%, not just
            match it. Independent coverage, including ConsumerAffairs, describes the same beat-by-5% policy.
            For a treadmill to qualify:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Identical product:</strong> the same brand and the same model number.</li>
            <li><strong>In stock at Academy</strong> in store or online at the time of purchase.</li>
            <li><strong>A current, verifiable price</strong> from a printed or digital ad, or a website. For
            an online match, Academy asks for the retailer's name and a direct link to the product.</li>
            <li><strong>From a qualifying retailer:</strong> any local retailer's printed ad, or one of the
            named online retailers — Amazon and Walmart (excluding third-party sellers on either), Bass Pro
            Shops, Cabela's, Carter's Country, Champs Sporting Goods, Dick's Sporting Goods, Dunham's Sports,
            Eastbay, Fanatics, Hibbett Sports, Kansas Sampler, Rally House, REI, Scheels, Sportsman's Warehouse
            and Target.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The exclusions matter for treadmills: misprinted prices, clearance, closeouts, timed events,
            buy-one-get-one offers, rebates, coupons, membership-only prices and limited-quantity offers are
            all excluded, and Academy may limit a match to one per customer per day per item. It will also
            match its own website price in store and vice versa, and it offers a <strong>price
            adjustment</strong> on items bought within 14 days of the date on your receipt, excluding
            clearance and timed-event purchases.
          </p>
          <p>
            Two practical notes. First, manufacturers' own websites, Best Buy, Costco and Home Depot are not
            on the online list, so a sale price on nordictrack.com, for example, does not qualify unless a
            local retailer prints it in an ad — and many brand sales are timed events in any case. Second,
            the identical-model rule is strict; compare the full item number before you ask. For when
            treadmill prices typically fall, see the
            <a href="/best-time-of-year-to-buy-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best time of year to buy a treadmill</a>
            and our notes on judging <a href="/treadmill-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Black Friday treadmill deals</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="credit-financing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">10. The Academy Credit Card and Paying Over Time</h2>
<p>
            In March 2026 Academy replaced its old store card with two new cards issued by Comenity Capital
            Bank, part of Bread Financial: the myAcademy Rewards Mastercard, usable anywhere, and the
            myAcademy Rewards Credit Card, usable only at Academy. You are considered for the Mastercard
            first and, if not eligible, for the store-only card. Bread Financial's announcement and
            Academy's card page agree on the core terms, as checked on 20 October 2026:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>5% off</strong> purchases at Academy made with either card, excluding gift cards,
            licences and in-store services.</li>
            <li><strong>$30 off</strong> a first purchase over $30 made on the day you are approved. Academy's
            terms say this cannot be combined with the 5% discount, so on a treadmill bought as your first
            card purchase the saving may be $30 rather than 5% — on a $1,299.99 machine that is a $35
            difference. Ask at checkout which applies.</li>
            <li><strong>Free shipping</strong> with no minimum, but bulk and select items are excluded, so
            it may not cover a treadmill.</li>
            <li><strong>No annual fee</strong>; a variable APR applies to any balance not paid in full. The
            card is not available to California residents.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The card is a discount tool, not a financing plan. We did not see a deferred-interest or
            0%-for-a-period promotion on Academy's card page, so carrying a treadmill balance on it means
            paying interest at the card's variable rate. Academy's checkout also accepts Klarna, Sezzle,
            PayPal and Bread Pay installment loans, which Academy lists as eligible for fitness equipment,
            and the treadmill pages we checked showed "Pay in 4 interest-free payments" alongside a
            monthly "as low as" figure. Read the terms of whichever plan you choose — the rate, the term
            and what happens on a return — before signing. Our guide to
            <a href="/treadmill-financing/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill financing</a>
            compares the main options.
          </p>
          <p>
            The product pages also offered optional protection plans — two- and three-year plans priced
            between $64.99 and $179 on the machines we checked. Read who administers a plan and how it
            overlaps with the manufacturer's warranty before adding one.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="compare-channels" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">11. How Do Academy's Prices Compare With Other Places to Buy?</h2>
<p>
            There is no simple answer, which is the point. On 20 October 2026 we compared two NordicTrack
            treadmills that carried the same model numbers at Academy and on NordicTrack's own site:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[480px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Model (item number)</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">academy.com</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">nordictrack.com</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T Series 10 (NTL15425)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,299.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,599.99 on sale (was $1,799.99), free standard delivery</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Commercial 1250 (NTL14125)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,999.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,599.99 on sale (was $1,999.99), free standard delivery</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            So Academy was $300 cheaper on one machine and $400 dearer on the other, before Academy's bulk
            delivery charge, which is calculated at checkout. NordicTrack's site also advertised a 30-day
            home trial. Neither channel was consistently cheaper, and both prices will have moved by the
            time you read this. Our review of the
            <a href="/nordictrack-commercial-1250-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">NordicTrack Commercial 1250</a>
            covers that machine in detail.
          </p>
          <p>
            Against other sporting goods chains, Academy works much like
            <a href="/dicks-sporting-goods-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Dick's Sporting Goods</a>
            or <a href="/scheels-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Scheels</a>: a mainstream range,
            some floor models, freight delivery for big machines. Its distinguishing features are the
            beat-by-5% price match, which lists Dick's and Scheels among the qualifying competitors, and
            a regional footprint in the South and Southeast where those chains are thinner on the ground.
            Against <a href="/walmart-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Walmart</a> and
            <a href="/buying-a-treadmill-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Amazon</a>, it has
            a smaller range but no third-party marketplace sellers, and a store to walk into.
          </p>
          <p>
            The sensible approach is the same everywhere: settle the specification, then compare the
            delivered price for the identical model number across channels, adding delivery level,
            assembly and return terms to the comparison. Our guide to
            <a href="/treadmills-for-sale/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmills for sale</a>
            sets out what each channel usually includes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="warranty-recalls" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">12. Who Handles the Warranty, and What About Recalls?</h2>
<p>
            Warranty cover on a treadmill bought at Academy comes from the manufacturer, and the product
            pages we checked listed the manufacturer's terms in the specifications — frame, motor, parts
            and labour separately. Claims, parts and in-home service generally run through the brand, so
            register the machine with the manufacturer, keep the model and serial numbers with your Academy
            receipt, and check whether the brand has service technicians where you live. Read the labour
            term in particular: Academy's T Series 10 listing and NordicTrack's own page both gave ten
            years on the frame, two years on parts and one year on labour. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-warranty-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">warranty guide</a>
            explains how to read the terms.
          </p>
          <p>
            We searched the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission's recall database on 20 October 2026 for
            every brand in the table above and found no treadmill recall for any of them. Three related
            recalls are worth knowing about: iFIT recalled NordicTrack rowing machines for a fire hazard in
            October 2025 and NordicTrack and ProForm 50 lb adjustable dumbbells in 2024, and Johnson Health
            Tech, which now owns Bowflex, recalled BowFlex adjustable dumbbells in June 2025. None of those is
            a treadmill. Academy also keeps a product recalls page on its site. Registering your treadmill
            with the manufacturer is how you would hear about any future recall.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="checklist" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">13. How Do You Judge a Treadmill at Academy, and What Should You Check Before Paying?</h2>
<p>
            Judge the machine on the same figures you would anywhere, not on the screen or the sale tag.
            Academy's specification lists include useful fields — continuous motor horsepower, running
            surface, maximum user weight and manufacturer warranty — but they are not always complete; the
            NordicTrack T Series 10 listing we read gave the running surface length (60 inches) without the
            width. Check gaps against the manufacturer's page.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Motor:</strong> continuous-duty horsepower, not peak. See the
            <a href="/treadmill-horsepower-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">horsepower guide</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Running surface:</strong> length and width against your stride and height. See the
            <a href="/treadmill-belt-size-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">belt size guide</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Subscription:</strong> many NordicTrack, ProForm, Bowflex and Echelon features need a
            paid membership. Check what the machine does without one; our guide to
            <a href="/best-treadmills-without-subscriptions/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmills without subscriptions</a>
            sets out the cost over time.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Before you pay, run through this list:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Tested, or researched properly:</strong> walked, run, inclined and folded in store,
            or read independent coverage of the exact model.</li>
            <li><strong>Item number confirmed</strong> against what you tried or researched.</li>
            <li><strong>Delivered price known:</strong> product price plus the bulk delivery charge for the
            level you want, compared with the delivered price elsewhere.</li>
            <li><strong>Delivery level chosen:</strong> door, main entrance or room of choice.</li>
            <li><strong>Assembly arranged:</strong> free for store pick-up on select models, or through the
            brand, a technician or yourself.</li>
            <li><strong>Return logistics understood:</strong> unused and boxed for a change-of-mind return,
            and Customer Care for bulk items.</li>
            <li><strong>Price match checked:</strong> identical model, qualifying retailer, not a timed event.</li>
            <li><strong>Card terms read:</strong> whether you would get $30 off or 5%, and the APR if you
            carry a balance.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If the specification fits and the numbers work, Academy is a sound place to buy. If you are
            still deciding how much to spend, start with our guide to
            <a href="/how-much-should-you-spend-on-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">how much to spend on a treadmill</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>


